    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43370" root="لقى" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِيَهُ</span></b>  <i>He met him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
<i>He</i> [<i>met with,</i> or] <i>found him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (Msb.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلْقاهُمٌ أُسْدًا</span> [<i>Thou will find them lions</i>].
(Mughnee, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّ</span>.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">??</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِيتُهُ</span> and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَاقَيْتُهُ</span></b>  <i>I came near to him, facing him: came
to face his face. near to him</i> (Ksh, in ii. 13.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِيَهُ بِمَكْرُوهِ</span> (K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حبه</span>, &amp;c.) <i>He</i>
[<i>encountered with him,</i> or <i>said to him,</i> or <i>did
to him, a thing disliked,</i> or <i>hated:</i> (TK in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جبه</span>:) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استقبلهُ بِمَا يَكْرَهُ</span>.

